          "text": "Here's what was causing the lag and what I fixed:\n\n**Root cause**: When you exit the app and come back, `CADisplayLink` (which drives the orb animations and waveform at ~10fps) auto-pauses in background, but **nothing was un-pausing it on foreground return**. The app had zero `scenePhase` handling. The orb, ripples, waveform bars, and ambient shimmer would all freeze until some other event (like a tab switch) happened to restart them.\n\n**Changes made**:\n\n1. **`ClassifySoundApp.swift` \u2014 `MainView`**: Added `@Environment(\\.scenePhase)` and an `onChange` handler that:\n   - On `.active`: Resumes the `AudioLevelMonitor` display link (un-pauses if still monitoring, or full-starts if detection is running but monitor was stopped)\n   - On `.background`: Pauses the display link to save CPU on invisible ticks\n\n2. **`AudioLevelMonitor.swift`**: Added two lightweight methods:\n   - `resumeFromBackground()` \u2014 just un-pauses the display link and resets the silence counter (no audio engine teardown/rebuild)\n   - `pauseForBackground()` \u2014 just pauses the display link (cheaper than `stopMonitoring()` which tears down everything)\n\nThis is much lighter than doing a full stop/start cycle \u2014 the audio engine and external feed state are preserved, so animations resume instantly when you return to the app."
